"""Approximate a sparse text-layout feature, not the meaning of the prose.

Negative spikes mark heading underlines and their closing newlines, especially
under headings with explicit Markdown section IDs. Blank lines suppress this
response. Smaller rules cover standalone opening braces, forum-profile labels,
diff headers, and caret runs. An en dash followed by a nonbreaking space gives
a positive spike. Elsewhere it predicts zero, apart from a small negative
baseline on space-led document-initial tokens. State keeps bounded copies of
the current and preceding line and resets at document boundaries.
