Negative responses mark 'no one/two', small numeral counts and units,
and collective 'you/we all'. Positive exceptions include reciprocal
fractions and 'one-sided', plus Chinese demonstratives following pronouns
or negation. Standalone small-integer lines have a negative ending.
The integer is accumulated across digit tokens; a document boundary
clears it and the previous word.
